{
  "_about": "Explain's check before the model (backend/llm/natlas_guard.py). A page that is about health or medicine, money or payments, or harm never reaches N-ATLaS: the app plays 'Please ask your teacher'. One 'strong' term is enough; otherwise two different 'words' of the same topic. Matching ignores case, tone marks and hooked letters (OCR loses them), whole words only. English health words: reviewed and extended by Dr. Amos (17 Nov 2026); his reasons are in \"_notes\". Hausa, Yorùbá and Igbo, and the money and harm lists: drafts by the developer, for native speakers to review. Over-blocking is the safe side.",
